# ── Trailing slash: handled natively by Next.js trailingSlash:true ────────────
# With output:"export" + trailingSlash:true, Next.js generates every page as
# slug/index.html. Netlify serves slug/index.html at /slug/ returning 200.
# The old catch-all rules below are REMOVED — they were redundant with the
# static file structure and could create loops in edge cases.
#
# REMOVED (redundant):
#   /routes/:slug /routes/:slug/ 301
#   /:state/:city/:service /:state/:city/:service/ 301
#   /:state/:city /:state/:city/ 301
#
# If Netlify ever needs a fallback for non-slash → slash, uncomment ONE rule:
